 "sentences": [
  {
   "t": 4.34,
   "end": 5.18,
   "text": "Namaskar"
  },
  {
   "t": 7.58,
   "end": 13.7,
   "text": "In the third sutra, we have seen that enlightenment by overcoming of opposites"
  },
  {
   "t": 13.7,
   "end": 19.62,
   "text": "can happen by entering the center between the two, which is void."
  },
  {
   "t": 20.8,
   "end": 26.6,
   "text": "The fourth sutra brings the theory and practice of overcoming dualities"
  },
  {
   "t": 26.6,
   "end": 32.46,
   "text": "down to its application to all the elements of worldly existence."
  },
  {
   "t": 33.88,
   "end": 41.02,
   "text": "In this, it follows the comprehensive scheme of the elements or principles of reality called tattva,"
  },
  {
